ants new gretchen that's how he found  out about this retreat  very odd that this story threat has  never picked up on for the rest of the  season then there's what happened to  nora it's highly implied that nora died  after trying to save her sister from the  shark attack a shark attack which  resulted in rachel losing her hand  nor is the only girl besides jeanette  who is not interviewed and rachel says  two interesting things about nora while  being interviewed  one she asked if her parents knew what  happened to nora  r.e her being dead and two you know what  i feel  it's her hand holding mine  the writers are wanting us to believe  she's dead but knowing how this show has  many twists and turns and nothing can be  ruled out one of the biggest mysteries  season one leaves us with is what  happens between the shark attack and  their extraction from the island  we never actually see leah expose nora  for being an operative  and the girls are separated as soon as  they leave so it's entirely possible  that none of the girls know about  nora's involvement in their captivity  then there's this question of  phase two when gretchen has asked what  to do about leah being held in that pit  she's also told that the rollout for  quote phase two  has absorbed all available watercraft  and it won't be until another three  hours that they can deal with leah  she also says this are you on your way  up top  yes supervision is my watch word this  time round  that's how we avoid any predicaments  this hints that gretchen likely has more  than one  island she's overseeing the first island  with the girls we've seen this season  was a failure hence why she's more  hands-on with this other one  and it could also explain why she went  to that rich donor to beg for more money  so phase two could actually mean three  things one a new island with new girls  two what the girls are currently going  through during these interviews  or three the twilight of adam during  lee's escape she un